All in One Facebook Manager. It integrates Facebook to your Site. Open Graph supported.

== Description ==
All in One Facebook Manager. It integrates Facebook in your Site. Flexo Facebook Manager have many Options, which will allow the User to Achieve optimal Social Network Integration. Currently, this Plugin supports:

1. Like Box
2. Comments Area
3. Open Graph Protocol
4. View customization
5. Different Options for personalization
6. Ability to store locally the count of Likes and Comments (for sorting etc.)
7. Multiple Languages support

This Plugin is working with Pages, Posts, Categories and Widgets.

For Demo, you can visit the URL bellow:
http://www.flexostudio.com/flexo-facebook-manager.html

PS: If you like this Plugin, dont forget to support us by giving a Rating

For more our Plugins see: http://www.flexostudio.com/wordpress-plugins-flexo-utils.html

== Installation ==
1.	Download.
2.	Unzip.
3.	Upload to the plugins directory.
4.	Activate the plugin.
5.	FILL YOUR App ID in the appId Input Field for proper work
6.	Have a nice work.

== How to use ==
Access and enter the necessary global data through the Dashboard Left Administration Pane.

Bellow each Page/Post you can find the plugin box, titled &Prime; Flexo Facebook Manager &Prime;, that allow different social personalization for each Page/Post. 

If you have additional Questions, write us at fb-manager@flexostudio.com

== Frequently Asked Questions ==
= How can i get App ID =

Visit https://developers.facebook.com/apps for App ID

= Is this plugin blocking WordPress Comments automatically =

No, this Plugin is not related to the WordPress Comments System

= Can i use Open Graph Protocol without using Like and Comments Areas =

Yes, you can. We have added this Option in v.1.0010

= I have already entered the most description information in &Prime; All in One SEO Pack &Prime;. Is there any way I can combine them both?  =

Yes, we have added Option that allow you to choose SEO Info in your Open Graph Description

= Is there any way i can propose new feature?  =

Yes, write us at fb-manager@flexostudio.com

= How I can add Facebook in The Category Page or somewhere? =

You can add Facebook arbitrarily in your code using the script bellow:

&lt;?php  flexoFBManager::get_form($id,$type); ?&gt;

$id can accept different values, depending where are you using the Function.
 It can be your CategoryID, PageID, PostID or CurrentURL(permalink).

= Options for $type are: =

* &prime;default &prime;-insert Likes and Comments
* &prime;like &prime;-only Likes
* &prime;comments &prime;-only Comments
* &prime;open_g &prime;-only Open Graph

